_accessor : Register a custom accessor on Series objects.\n258 |     register_index_accessor : Register a custom accessor on Index objects.\n259 | \n260 |     Notes\n261 |     -----\n262 |     This function allows you to register a custom-defined accessor class for {klass}.\n263 |     The requirements for the accessor class are as follows:\n264 | \n265 |     * Must contain an init method that:\n266 | \n267 |       * accepts a single {klass} object\n268 | \n269 |       * raises an AttributeError if the {klass} object does not have correctly\n270 |         matching inputs for the accessor\n271 | \n272 |     * Must contain a method for each access pattern.\n273 | \n274 |       * The methods should be able to take any argument signature.\n275 | \n276 |       * Accessible using the @property decorator if no additional arguments are\n277 |         needed.\n278 | \n279 |     Examples\n280 |     --------\n281 |     {examples}\n282 |     \"\"\"\n283 | \n284 |     def decorator(accessor: TypeT) -> TypeT:\n285 |         if hasattr(cls, name):\n286 |             warnings.warn(\n287 |                 f\"registration of accessor {accessor!r} under name \"\n288 |                 f\"{name!r} for type {cls!r} is overriding a preexisting \"\n289 |                 f\"attribute with the same name.\",\n290 |                 UserWarning,\n291 |                 stacklevel=find_stack_level(),\n292 |             )\n293 |         setattr(cls, name, Accessor(name, accessor))\n294 |         cls._accessors.add(name)\n295 |         return accessor\n296 | \n297 |     return decorator\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/accessor.py:register_dataframe_accessor`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n327 | def register_dataframe_accessor(name: str) -> Callable[[TypeT], TypeT]:\n328 |     from pandas import DataFrame\n329 | \n330 |     return _register_accessor(name, DataFrame)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/accessor.py:register_series_accessor`.\nSource: Retrieved c